subject: fix(security): shutdown endpoint auth bypass (GAP-P0-02)

Primary gate: dashboardGuard auth (JWT session or CLI machine-id token).
Secondary gate: SHUTDOWN_SECRET env var (defence-in-depth when set).

Previously, if SHUTDOWN_SECRET was unset (common), any network-reachable
client could POST /api/shutdown and kill the server. The middleware layer
marks this path as ALWAYS_PROTECTED, but the route handler lacked its own
defence-in-depth check.

Adds vitest.config.mjs for @/ alias resolution in unit tests.
10 unit tests covering: no-auth reject, CLI-token accept, JWT accept,
wrong-token reject, SHUTDOWN_SECRET secondary gate, production block.

Refs: docs/plans-and-prompts/research/9router/32-gap-analysis-comprehensive.md

